    "solution": "From the smoke, parry the bolt right through the empty casting frame into the distant coil. Drop beside the carriage and hold Grab to catch its lower ring. The freight roof leaves no standing clearance. Hold Up with Grab to shorten the chain over the first low teeth; pay out with Down in the wide gap to pass below the hanging teeth; reel in again before the last low teeth. Jump-release onto the broad receiving shelf and climb to the anvil. Make a small jump and downward cut to reach the high return gallery. Let the gale carry you back into the casting pocket. A left cut sets the screen and its small rear guard; the guard stops later shots while the main screen blocks the watchlight. Hop left into the starting smoke and follow the long shadow home.",
    "nearestExisting": "B29 combines transported shade with a returned shot, B30 casts shade during a swing, and B12 replaces a temporary shield. Here a shot can cross the gale that prevents the knight from reaching the casting face. Its coil releases both the lower carriage and the home door; a lower ride and upper anvil return approach the same frame from its useful side before the final walk uses its permanent shadow.",
    "novelty": "The shared passage has three different uses at three heights: a bolt travels upwind through the empty frame, a carrier takes the knight below the thorn-covered firing lane, and the anvil returns the knight above that same lane into the casting pocket. Only then can the frame become the screen needed for the long downwind home route.",
