    },
    "endingForgiveness": "The rope-height changes each have a six-tile transition gap; four-frame earlier and later payout variants pass. The receiving shelf is six tiles wide and allows a normal climb to the anvil. The casting pocket gains a visible rear guard with the same cut, preventing a late bolt from making the ending depend on arrival phase. A three-second rest behind the completed screen passes.",
    "designNotes": "Only B52 opts into watchClarity presentation. The roof leaves eight pixels over the carrier—enough for the deck but not the knight. Alternating floor/hanging/floor teeth make rope length consequential. The original top-riding tape and fixed-rope alternatives fail. Grab is remappable: hold Grab; Up reels in; Down pays out; Jump releases. Added one visible mould cell in the casting pocket to shelter the delayed final jump from later shots.",
